P.‚Äù","code","‚ÄúRobust Conversational Agents against Imperceptible Toxicity Triggers.‚Äù","‚ÄúUniversal and Transferable Adversarial Attacks on Aligned Language Models.‚Äù","‚ÄúRLPrompt: Optimizing Discrete Text Prompts with Reinforcement Learning.‚Äù","‚ÄúIs BERT Really Robust? A Strong Baseline for Natural Language Attack on Text Classification and Entailment.‚Äù","‚ÄúBERT-Attack: Adversarial Attack Against BERT Using BERT.‚Äù","\"TextAttack: A Framework for Adversarial Attacks, Data Augmentation, and Adversarial Training in NLP.\"","‚ÄúBot-Adversarial Dialogue for Safe Conversational Agents.‚Äù","‚ÄúAdversarial training for high-stakes reliability.‚Äù","‚ÄúRed Teaming Language Models to Reduce Harms: Methods, Scaling Behaviors, and Lessons Learned.‚Äù","‚ÄúRed Teaming Language Models with Language Models.‚Äù","‚ÄúRed Teaming Language Models to Reduce Harms: Methods, Scaling Behaviors, and Lessons Learned.‚Äù","‚ÄúFLIRT: Feedback Loop In-context Red Teaming.‚Äù","‚ÄúExplore, Establish, Exploit: Red Teaming Language Models from Scratch.‚Äù","‚ÄúDefending ChatGPT against Jailbreak Attack via Self-Reminder.‚Äù","‚ÄúAutomatically Auditing Large Language Models via Discrete Optimization.‚Äù","‚ÄúCompromising Real-World LLM-Integrated Applications with Indirect Prompt Injection.‚Äù","‚ÄúBaseline Defenses for Adversarial Attacks Against Aligned Language Models.‚Äù","‚ÄúJailbroken: How Does LLM Safety Training Fail?‚Äù","‚ÄúEDA: Easy data augmentation techniques for boosting performance on text classification tasks.‚Äù","www.jailbreakchat.com","‚ÄúYou can use GPT-4 to create prompt injections against GPT-4‚Äù","Nlp","Language-Model","Safety","Adversarial Attacks","Robustness","Redteam"],"url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-10-25-adv-attack-llm/","chroma:document":"Zou et al. (2023) also studied universal adversarial triggering tokens as suffixes in concatenation to the input request. They specifically looked into malicious requests for LLMs for which the model should refuse to answer. In fact, refusal on disallowed content categories such as criminal advice is one important safety mitigation built into GPT-4 (OpenAI 2023). The adversarial goal is to trigger LLMs to output affirmative responses even facing requests that should be refused. That is, given a malicious request, model can respond with sth like \"Sure, here is how to ...\". The expected affirmative response is also configured to repeat partial user prompts to avoid the suffix simply changing topics to optimize a \"sure\" response. The loss function is simply the NLL of outputting target response.","element_id":"2775507ceeaaa257529304164be2b816","category":"CompositeElement","emphasized_text_tags":["b","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","i","i","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","b","b","i","b","i","i","i","b","b","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","i"],"emphasized_text_contents":["black box","What","NOUN","‚ÜíWhich","NOUN","WP","is ‚Üí","WP","‚Äôs‚Äô","was‚Üíis","GBDA","make adversarial loss optimization differentiable","extreme","‚Äúa similarity score for evaluating text generation that captures the semantic similarity between pairwise tokens in contextualized embeddings of a transformer model.‚Äù","HotFlip","Universal Adversarial Triggers","UAT","AutoPrompt","UAT-LM","UTSC","unigram","affirmative","greedy coordinate gradient (GCG)","transferability","ARCA","coordinate ascent","should have been mitigated","Competing objective","Mismatched generalization","Display of saliency score of each token","Token substitution and insertion","Zero-shot generation","Stochastic few-shot generation","Supervised learning","Reinforcement learning","Explore","Establish","Exploit","FLIRT","update in-context exemplars","FIFO","LIFO","the last one","Scoring","effectiveness","diversity","low-toxicity","Scoring-LIFO","robust","inner maximization","outer minimization","Inner maximization","Outer minimization","instruct","adversarial training","Paraphrase","Retokenization"],"filetype":"text/html","languages":["eng"],"link_urls":["#token-manipulation","https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.05909","https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/P18-1079/","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2022-04-15-data-gen/#EDA","https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11196","https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.11932","https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.500.pdf","#gradient-based-attacks","https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13733","https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.01144","https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.09675","https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.06751","https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07125","#hotflip","https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.15980","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.02392","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.15043","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.08774","#UAT","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.04381","#jailbreak-prompting","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","www.jailbreakchat.com/prompt/3d318387-903a-422c-8347-8e12768c14b5","www.jailbreakchat.com/prompt/4f37a029-9dff-4862-b323-c96a5504de5d","https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/bNCDexejSZpkuu3yz/you-can-use-gpt-4-to-create-prompt-injections-against-gpt-4","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.12173","#humans-in-the-loop-red-teaming","https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02701","https://sites.google.com/view/qanta/resources","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.01663","https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02701","#BERT-Attack","https://aclanthology.org/2021.naacl-main.235/","https://github.com/facebookresearch/ParlAI/tree/main/parlai/tasks/bot_adversarial_dialogue","https://www.tensorflow.org/datasets/catalog/bot_adversarial_dialogue","https://github.com/anthropics/hh-rlhf/tree/master/red-team-attempts","https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07858","https://cdn.openai.com/papers/gpt-4.pdf","https://cdn.openai.com/papers/DALL_E_3_System_Card.pdf","#model-red-teaming","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2018-04-08-policy-gradient/#a2c","https://github.com/facebookresearch/ParlAI/tree/main/parlai/tasks/bot_adversarial_di