␀ p␀a␀s␀s␀ ␀{"url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-10-25-adv-attack-llm/","emphasized_text_tags":["b","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","i","i","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","b","b","i","b","i","i","i","b","b","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","i"],"languages":["eng"],"category":"CompositeElement","chroma:document":"ARCA (‚ÄúAutoregressive Randomized Coordinate Ascent‚Äù; Jones et al. 2023) considers a broader set of optimization problems to find input-output pairs $(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y})$ that match certain behavior pattern; such as non-toxic input starting with \"Barack Obama\" but leading to toxic output. Given an auditing objective $\\phi: \\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathbb{R}$ that maps a pair of (input prompt, output completion) into scores. Examples of behavior patterns captured by $\\phi$ are as follows:\n\nDerogatory comments about celebrities: $\\phi(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}) = \\texttt{StartsWith}(\\mathbf{x}, [\\text{celebrity}]) + \\texttt{NotToxic}(\\mathbf{x}) + \\texttt{Toxic}(\\mathbf{y})$.","emphasized_text_contents":["black box","What","NOUN","‚ÜíWhich","NOUN","WP","is ‚Üí","WP","‚Äôs‚Äô","was‚Üíis","GBDA","make adversarial loss optimization differentiable","extreme","‚Äúa similarity score for evaluating text generation that captures the semantic similarity between pairwise tokens in contextualized embeddings of a transformer model.‚Äù","HotFlip","Universal Adversarial Triggers","UAT","AutoPrompt","UAT-LM","UTSC","unigram","affirmative","greedy coordinate gradient (GCG)","transferability","ARCA","coordinate ascent","should have been mitigated","Competing objective","Mismatched generalization","Display of saliency score of each token","Token substitution and insertion","Zero-shot generation","Stochastic few-shot generation","Supervised learning","Reinforcement learning","Explore","Establish","Exploit","FLIRT","update in-context exemplars","FIFO","LIFO","the last one","Scoring","effectiveness","diversity","low-toxicity","Scoring-LIFO","robust","inner maximization","outer minimization","Inner maximization","Outer minimization","instruct","adversarial training","Paraphrase","Retokenization"],"orig_elements":"","filetype":"text/html","link_texts":["#","Morris et al. 2020","Ribeiro et al (2018)","EDA","Wei & Zou 2019","Jin et al. 2019","Li et al. 2020","#","Guo et al. 2021","Jang et al. 2016","Zhang et al. 2019","Ebrahimi et al. 2018","Wallace et al. (2019)","HotFlip","Shin et al., 2020","Mehrabi et al. (2022)","Zou et al. (2023)","OpenAI 2023","UAT and AutoPrompt","Jones et al. 2023","#","Wei et al. (2023)","DAN","AIM","it can understand","Wei et al. (2023)","Greshake et al. (2023)","#","Wallace et al. (2019)","QuizBowl QA dataset","Ziegler et al. (2022)","Wallace et al. (2019)","BERT-Attack","Xu et al. 2021","BAD dataset","Tensorflow dataset","red-teaming dataset","Ganguli, et al. 2022","GPT-4","DALL-E 3","#","Perez et al. 2022","A2C","BAD (Bot Adversarial Dialogue) dataset","nucleus sampling","Casper et al. (2023)","Perez et al. (2022)","here","here","here","Mehrabi et al. 2023","in-context learning","Perez et al. 2022","Schramowski et al. 2022","https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet)","Perspective API","#","#","Madry et al. 2017","#","Xie et al. 2023","Jain et al. 2023","White-box attacks","UAT-LM","Jain et al. 2023","#","#","‚ÄúTowards Deep Learning Models Resistant to Adversarial Attacks‚Äù","‚ÄúSemantically equivalent adversarial rules for debugging NLP models‚Äù","‚ÄúGradient-based adversarial attacks against text transformers‚Äù","‚ÄúHotFlip: White-Box Adversarial Examples for Text Classification‚Äù","‚ÄúUniversal Adversarial Triggers for Attacking and Analyzing NLP.‚Äù","code","‚ÄúRobust Conversational Agents against Imperceptible Toxicity Triggers.‚Äù","‚ÄúUniversal and Transferable Adversarial Attacks on Aligned Language Models.‚Äù","‚ÄúRLPrompt: Optimizing Discrete Text Prompts with Reinforcement Learning.‚Äù","‚ÄúIs BERT Really Robust? A Strong Baseline for Natural Language Attack on Text Classification and Entailment.‚Äù","‚ÄúBERT-Attack: Adversarial Attack Against BERT Using BERT.‚Äù","\"TextAttack: A Framework for Adversarial Attacks, Data Augmentation, and Adversarial Training in NLP.\"","‚ÄúBot-Adversarial Dialogue for Safe Conversational Agents.‚Äù","‚ÄúAdversarial training for high-stakes reliability.‚Äù","‚ÄúRed Teaming Language Models to Reduce Harms: Methods, Scaling Behaviors, and Lessons Learned.‚Äù","‚ÄúRed Teaming Language Models with Language Models.‚Äù","‚ÄúRed Teaming Language Models to Reduce Harms: Methods, Scaling Behaviors, and Lessons Learned.‚Äù","‚ÄúFLIRT: Feedback Loop In-context Red Teaming.‚Äù","‚ÄúExplore, Establish, Exploit: Red Teaming Language Models from Scratch.‚Äù","‚ÄúDefending ChatGPT against Jailbreak Attack via Self-Reminder.‚Äù","‚ÄúAutomatically Auditing Large Language Models via Discrete Optimization.‚Äù","‚ÄúCompromising Real-World LLM-Integrated Applications with Indirect Prompt Injection.‚Äù","‚ÄúBaseline Defenses for Adversarial Attacks Against Aligned Language Models.‚Äù","‚ÄúJailbroken: How Does LLM Safety Training Fail?‚Äù","‚ÄúEDA: Easy data augmentation techniques for boosting performance on text classification tasks.‚Äù","www.jailbreakchat.com","‚ÄúYou can use GPT-4 to create prompt injections against GPT-4‚Äù","Nlp","Language-Model","Safety","Adversarial Attacks","Robustness","Redteam"],"link_urls":["#token-manipulation","https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.05909","https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/P18-1079/","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2022-04-15-data-gen/#EDA","https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11196","https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.11932","https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.500.pdf","#gradient-based-attacks","https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13733","https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.01144","https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.09675","https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.06751","https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07125","#hotflip","https://arxiv.org/a