\\mathbf{y}) \\in \\mathcal{X} \\times \\mathcal{Y}}\\;\\phi(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}) + \\lambda_\\text{LLM}\\;\\log p ( \\mathbf{y} \\mid \\mathbf{x}) $$\n\nwhere $\\lambda_\\text{LLM}$ is a hyperparameter instead of a variable. And we have $\\log p ( \\mathbf{y} \\mid \\mathbf{x}) = \\sum_{i=1}^n p(y_i \\mid x, y_1, \\dots, y_{i-1})$.\n\nThe coordinate ascent algorithm of ARCA updates only one token at index $i$ at each step to maximize the above objective, while other tokens are fixed. The process iterates through all the token positions until $p(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{y}$ and $\\phi(.) \\geq \\tau$, or hit the iteration limit.","url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-10-25-adv-attack-llm/","emphasized_text_contents":["black box","What","NOUN","‚ÜíWhich","NOUN","WP","is ‚Üí","WP","‚Äôs‚Äô","was‚Üíis","GBDA","make adversarial loss optimization differentiable","extreme","‚Äúa similarity score for evaluating text generation that captures the semantic similarity between pairwise tokens in contextualized embeddings of a transformer model.‚Äù","HotFlip","Universal Adversarial Triggers","UAT","AutoPrompt","UAT-LM","UTSC","unigram","affirmative","greedy coordinate gradient (GCG)","transferability","ARCA","coordinate ascent","should have been mitigated","Competing objective","Mismatched generalization","Display of saliency score of each token","Token substitution and insertion","Zero-shot generation","Stochastic few-shot generation","Supervised learning","Reinforcement learning","Explore","Establish","Exploit","FLIRT","update in-context exemplars","FIFO","LIFO","the last one","Scoring","effectiveness","diversity","low-toxicity","Scoring-LIFO","robust","inner maximization","outer minimization","Inner maximization","Outer minimization","instruct","adversarial training","Paraphrase","Retokenization"],"orig_elements":""}␀␀␀HC ␀␀␀êC ␀␀␀pHC ␀␀␀‡C ␀␀␀êHC ␀␀␀‘B ␀␀␀∞HC ␀␀␀@‘B ␀␀␀–HC ␀␀␀p‘B ␀␀␀HC ␀␀␀0C ␀␀␀IC ␀␀␀ÄC ␀␀␀0IC ␀␀␀–C ␀␀␀PIC ␀␀␀†‘B ␀␀␀pIC