eration","https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.04265","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.06675","https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet)","https://perspectiveapi.com/","#peek-into-mitigation","#saddle-point-problem","https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06083","#some-work-on-llm-robustness","https://assets.researchsquare.com/files/rs-2873090/v1_covered_3dc9af48-92ba-491e-924d-b13ba9b7216f.pdf?c=1686882819","https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00614v2","#gradient-based-attacks","#UAT-LM","https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00614v2","#citation","#references","https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06083","https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/P18-1079/","https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13733","https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.06751","https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07125","https://github.com/Eric-Wallace/universal-triggers","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.02392","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.15043","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.12548","https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.11932","https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.500","https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.05909","https://aclanthology.org/2021.naacl-main.235/","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.01663","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07858","https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.04265","https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.09442","https://assets.researchsquare.com/files/rs-2873090/v1_covered_3dc9af48-92ba-491e-924d-b13ba9b7216f.pdf?c=1686882819","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.04381","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.12173","https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00614v2","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11196","www.jailbreakchat.com","https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/bNCDexejSZpkuu3yz/you-can-use-gpt-4-to-create-prompt-injections-against-gpt-4","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/nlp/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/language-model/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/safety/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/adversarial-attacks/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/robustness/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/redteam/"],"element_id":"2775507ceeaaa257529304164be2b816","chroma:document":"Only $s^\\text{lin}_i$ is approximated by first-order Taylor using the average embeddings of a random set of tokens instead of computing the delta with an original value like in HotFlip, UAT or AutoPrompt. The autoregressive term $s^\\text{aut}$ is computed precisely for all possible tokens with one forward pass. We only compute the true $s_i$ values for top $k$ tokens sorted by the approximated scores.\n\nExperiment on reversing prompts for toxic outputs:\n\nJailbreak Prompting#\n\nJailbreak prompts adversarially trigger LLMs to output harmful content that should have been mitigated. Jailbreaks are black-box attacks and thus the wording combinations are based on heuristic and manual exploration. Wei et al. (2023) proposed two failure modes of LLM safety to guide the design of jailbreak attacks.\n\nCompeting objective: This refers to a scenario when a model‚Äôs capabilities (E.g. \"should always follow instructions\") and safety goals conflict. Examples of jailbreak attacks that exploit competing objectives include:","filetype":"text/html"}␀␀␀{"languages":["eng"],"emphasized_text_contents":["black box","What","NOUN","‚ÜíWhich","NOUN","WP","is ‚Üí","WP","‚Äôs‚Äô","was‚Üíis","GBDA","make adversarial loss optimization differentiable","extreme","‚Äúa similarity score for evaluating text generation that captures the semantic similarity between pairwise tokens in contextualized embeddings of a transformer model.‚Äù","HotFlip","Universal Adversarial Triggers","UAT","AutoPrompt","UAT-LM","UTSC","unigram","affirmative","greedy coordinate gradient (GCG)","transferability","ARCA","coordinate ascent","should have been mitigated","Competing objective","Mismatched generalization","Display of saliency score of each token","Token substitution and insertion","Zero-shot generation","Stochastic few-shot generation","Supervised learning","Reinforcement learning","Explore","Establish","Exploit","FLIRT","update in-context exemplars","FIFO","LIFO","the last one","Scoring","effectiveness","diversity","low-toxicity","Scoring-LIFO","robust","inner maximization","outer minimization","Inner maximization","Outer minimization","instruct","adversarial training","Paraphrase","Retokenization"],"emphasized_text_tags":["b","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","i","i","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","b","b","i","b","i","i","i","b","b","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","i"],"link_urls":["#token-manipulation","https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.05909","https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/P18-1079/","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2022-04-15-data-gen/#EDA","https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11196","https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.11932","https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.500.pdf","#gradient-based-attacks","https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13733","https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.01144","https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.09675","https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.06751","https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07125","#hotflip","https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.15980","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.02392","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.15043","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.08774","#UAT","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.04381","#jailbreak-prompting","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","www.jailbreakchat.com/prompt/3d318387-903a-422c-8347-8e12768c14b5","www.jailbreakchat.com/prompt/4f37a029-9dff-4862-b323-c96a5504de5d","https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/bNCDexejSZpkuu3yz/you-can-use-gpt-4-to-create-prompt-injections-against-gpt-4","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.12173","#humans-in-the-loop-red-teaming","https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02701","https://sites.google.com/view/qanta/resources","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.01663","https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02701","#BERT-Attack","https://aclanthology.org/2021.naacl-main.235/","https://github.com/facebookresearch/ParlAI/tree/main/parlai/tasks/bot_adversarial_dialogue","https://www.tensorflow.org/datasets/catalog/bot_adversarial_dialogue","https://github.com/anthropics/hh-rlhf/tree/master/red-team-attempts","https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07858","https://cdn.openai.com/papers/gpt-4.pdf","https://cdn.openai.com/papers/DALL_E_3_System_Card.pdf","#model-red-teaming","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2018-04-08-policy-gradient/#a2c","https://github.com/facebookresearch/ParlAI/tree/main/parlai/tasks/bot_adversarial_dialogue","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2021-01-02-controllable-text-generation/#nucleus","https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.09442","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.15056","https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.14387","https://openai.com/blog/using-gpt-4-for-content-moderation","https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.04265","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.06675","https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet)","https://perspectiveapi.com/","#peek-into-mitigation","#saddle-point-problem","https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06083","#some-work-on-llm-robustness","https://assets.researchsquare.com/files/rs-2873090/v1_covered_3dc9af48-92ba-491e-924d-b13ba9b7216f.pdf?c=1686882819","https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00614v2","#gradient-based-attacks","#UAT-LM","https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00614v2","#citation","#references","https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06083","https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/P18-1079/","https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13733","https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.06751","https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07125","https://github.com/Eric-Wallace/universal-triggers","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.02392","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.15043","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.12548","https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.11932","https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.500","https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.05909","https://aclanthology.org/2021.naacl-main.235/","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.01663","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07858","https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.04265","https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.09442","https://assets.researchsquare.com/files/rs-2873090/v1_covered_3dc9af48-92ba-491e-924d-b13ba9b7216f.pdf?c=1686882819","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.04381","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.12173","https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00614v2","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11196","www.jailbreakchat.com","https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/bNCDexejSZpkuu3yz/you-can-use-gpt-4-to-create-prompt-injections-against-gpt-4","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/nlp/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/language-model/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/safety/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/adversarial-attacks/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/robustness/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/redteam/"],"chroma:document":"Prefix Injection: Ask the model to start with an affirmative confirmation.\n\nRefusal suppression: Give the model detailed instruction not to respond in refusal format.\n\nStyle injection: Ask the model not to use long words, and thus the model cannot do professional writing to give disclaimers or explain refusal.\n\nOthers: Role-play as DAN (Do Anything Now), AIM (always intelligent and Machiavellian), etc.\n\nMismatched generalization: Safety training fails to generalize to a domain for which capabilities exist. This happens when inputs are OOD for a model‚Äôs safety training data but within the scope of its broad pretraining corpus. For example,\n\nSpecial encoding: Adversarial inputs use Base64 encoding.\n\nCharacter transformation: ROT13 cipher, leetspeak (replacing letters with visually similar numbers and symbols), Morse code\n\nWord transformation: Pig Latin (replacing sensitive words with synonyms such as ‚Äúpilfer‚Äù instead of ‚Äústeal‚Äù), payload splitting (a.k.a. ‚Äútoken smuggling‚Äù to split sensitive words into substrings).","filetype":"text/html","category":"CompositeElement","element_id":"2775507ceeaaa257529304164be2b816","lin