"https://openai.com/blog/using-gpt-4-for-content-moderation","https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.04265","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.06675","https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet)","https://perspectiveapi.com/","#peek-into-mitigation","#saddle-point-problem","https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06083","#some-work-on-llm-robustness","https://assets.researchsquare.com/files/rs-2873090/v1_covered_3dc9af48-92ba-491e-924d-b13ba9b7216f.pdf?c=1686882819","https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00614v2","#gradient-based-attacks","#UAT-LM","https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00614v2","#citation","#references","https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06083","https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/P18-1079/","https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13733","https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.06751","https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07125","https://github.com/Eric-Wallace/universal-triggers","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.02392","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.15043","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.12548","https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.11932","https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.500","https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.05909","https://aclanthology.org/2021.naacl-main.235/","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.01663","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07858","https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.04265","https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.09442","https://assets.researchsquare.com/files/rs-2873090/v1_covered_3dc9af48-92ba-491e-924d-b13ba9b7216f.pdf?c=1686882819","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.04381","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.12173","https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00614v2","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11196","www.jailbreakchat.com","https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/bNCDexejSZpkuu3yz/you-can-use-gpt-4-to-create-prompt-injections-against-gpt-4","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/nlp/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/language-model/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/safety/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/adversarial-attacks/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/robustness/","https://lilianweng.github.io/tags/redteam/"],"element_id":"2775507ceeaaa257529304164be2b816","orig_elements":"","chroma:document":"Prompt-level obfuscations: Translation to other languages, asking the model to obfuscate in a way that it can understand\n\nWei et al. (2023) experimented a large of jailbreak methods, including combined strategies, constructed by following the above principles.\n\ncombination_1 composes prefix injection, refusal suppression, and the Base64 attack\n\ncombination_2 adds style injection\n\ncombination_3 adds generating website content and formatting constraints\n\nGreshake et al. (2023) make some high-level observations of prompt injection attacks. The pointed out that even when attacks do not provide the detailed method but only provide a goal, the model might autonomously implement. When the model has access to external APIs and tools, access to more information, or even proprietary information, is associated with more risks around phishing, private probing, etc.\n\nHumans in the Loop Red-teaming#","url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-10-25-adv-attack-llm/","filetype":"text/html"}␀␀␀","url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-06-23-agent/","emphasized_text_contents":["Planning","Memory","Tool use","Chain of thought","Tree of Thoughts","LLM+P","ReAct","Reflexion","decide to reset","Chain of Hindsight","Algorithm Distillation","algorithm","Sensory Memory","Short-Term Memory","Working Memory","Long-Term Memory","approximate nearest neighbors (ANN)‚Äã","LSH","hashing","ANNOY","random projection trees","HNSW","FAISS","clustering","ScaNN","anisotropic vector quantization","MRKL","knowing when to and how to use the tools are crucial","TALM","Toolformer","HuggingGPT","(1) Task planning","(2) Model selection","(3) Task execution","(4) Response generation","API-Bank","call the API","retrieve the API","plan API beyond retrieve and call","ChemCrow","Generative Agents","Memory","observation","Retrieval","Reflection","higher-level summaries of past events","Planning & Reacting","Finite context length","Challenges in long-term planning and task decomposition","Reliability of natural language interface"],"emphasized_text_tags":["b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","b","b","i","b","i","b","i","b","b","i","b","i","b","i","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","i","i","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","b","b"],"category":"CompositeElement","filetype":"text/html","chroma:document":"Constraints:\n1. ~4000 word limit for short term memory. Your short term memory is short, so immediately save important information to files.\n2. If you are unsure how you previously did something or want to recall past events, thinking about similar events will help you remember.\n3. No user assistance\n4. Exclusively use the commands listed in double quotes e.g. \"command name\"\n5. Use subprocesses for commands that will not terminate within a few minutes","element_id":"ed550bf6e7f15344c4ec2b455bfe14ea","link_urls":["https://github.com/Significant-Gravitas/Auto-GPT","https://github.com/AntonOsika/gpt-engineer","https://github.com/yoheinakajima/babyagi","#agent-system-overview","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/","#component-one-planning","#task-decomposition","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/#chain-of-thought-cot","https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.11903","https://{"element_id":"2775507ceeaaa257529304164be2b816","link_texts":["#","Morris et al. 2020","Ribeiro et al (2018)","EDA","Wei & Zou 2019","Jin et al. 2019","Li et al. 2020","#","Guo et al. 2021","Jang et al. 2016","Zhang et al. 2019","Ebrahimi et al. 2018","Wallace et al. (2019)","HotFlip","Shin et al., 2020","Mehrabi et al. (2022)","Zou et al. (2023)","OpenAI 2023","UAT and AutoPrompt","Jones et al. 2023","#","Wei et al. (2023)","DAN","AIM","it can understand","Wei et al. (2023)","Greshake et al. (2023)","#","Wallace et al. (20